# Tic Tac Flic Flac Floe - an abstract strategy game

The game is played on a standard 3x3 "tic tac toe" grid.

However, instead of just X and O, there are also T and S.

At the start of the game, one player picks XT and the other
player picks OS. These are the symbols they can draw.

Play progresses by players taking turns drawing one of their
symbols on the board. If an X (symmetrically, T) is present
in a grid square, an O cannot be placed (symmetrically, S),
and viseversa -- an O (S) blocks an X (T) from being placed.

The game ends when nobody can draw a symbol.

Part of this project is to explore different win conditions.

The original win condition (to be explored) is "the player
with the most three-in-a-rows".

## Questions

- Do players always have an available move until the board is filled?
- Is this equivalent to two parallel regular tic-tac-toes?
- Is the game balanced? Is there first player advantage?
- Can we solve the game, or force draws like in tictactoe?
- What symmetries exist.
